define-integration-settings-in-shared-types

Lane: cross

Unit: configure-integrations-through-shared-file

ChildPatch: define-integration-settings-in-shared-types

Form: GitDiff

Segment: schema

Purpose: Configure Proxy, GitHub and Telegram independently through one private integrations.json document.

Requires: none

Provides: Own shared proxy configuration and Telegram subscription types, separate service settings, redacted diagnostics, validated startup loading, and serialized atomic section updates that preserve other services and the last valid state on failure.

Boundary: Proxy validation and activation, GitHub querying and monitoring, Telegram delivery and dialogs remain with their service owners; missing configuration disables services, invalid configuration fails explicitly, and legacy files have no reader or migration route.

Verification: integrations tests cover independent settings, private file permissions, concurrent section preservation, failed writes, symlink rejection and secret-free errors; service tests cover startup activation and configuration consumers.

CrossGroup: control-center


